<section class="pr-sec rcost-sec" style="background:var(--ghost-grey,#f6f7fc)"><div class="section-inner">
<div class="rv"><div class="section-tag"><span class="s">&#10022;</span>What is really at stake</div><h2 class="section-title">The real cost is <em>rarely the price</em></h2>
<p class="section-sub">Choosing the wrong partner does not hurt today. It hurts six months later, when you are paying again to fix what should have been right the first time. Here is what is actually at stake.</p></div>
<div class="rcost-grid"><div class="rcost rv"><div class="rcost-bad"><span class="rcost-lab">The hidden cost</span><h4>The &ldquo;cheap&rdquo; that gets expensive</h4><p>A low rate and a loose scope feel safe, until the invoice creeps up, the deadline slips, and you have no way to push back.</p></div><div class="rcost-good"><span class="rcost-lab">With Brand Method</span><h4>Fixed price, in writing</h4><p>A set price and a clear deadline agreed up front, backed by a full refund if we miss either.</p></div></div><div class="rcost rv"><div class="rcost-bad"><span class="rcost-lab">Paying twice</span><h4>Paying to do it twice</h4><p>A logo that looks fine on one screen falls apart on signage, packaging and dark mode. Rebranding later costs three times more.</p></div><div class="rcost-good"><span class="rcost-lab">With Brand Method</span><h4>Built once, built right</h4><p>A complete system that holds up everywhere it shows up, so you never have to start over.</p></div></div><div class="rcost rv"><div class="rcost-bad"><span class="rcost-lab">The silence</span><h4>When it suddenly goes quiet</h4><p>Freelancers disappear halfway through. Agencies hand you to a junior the day you sign. When something breaks, the replies stop.</p></div><div class="rcost-good"><span class="rcost-lab">With Brand Method</span><h4>Always one call away</h4><p>One dedicated project manager who replies within two hours, every time, enforced as an SOP.</p></div></div><div class="rcost rv"><div class="rcost-bad"><span class="rcost-lab">Ownership</span><h4>Work you do not even own</h4><p>Many hand over flat files and quietly keep the source. Every future tweak means going back to them, and paying again.</p></div><div class="rcost-good"><span class="rcost-lab">With Brand Method</span><h4>Everything is yours</h4><p>You own every file and the full system behind it, with nothing locked away, ever.</p></div></div></div></div></section>
<section class="pr-sec faq-sec"><div class="section-inner"><div class="faq-card"><div class="faq-card-bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
<div class="rv"><div class="section-tag"><span class="s">&#10022;</span>Before you start</div><h2 class="section-title">Questions before <em>every project</em></h2>
<p class="section-sub">The things founders always ask before they start. Answered directly, no fluff.</p></div>
<div class="faq-list rv"><details class="faq-item"><summary>How does the money-back guarantee actually work?<span class="faq-ico"></span></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>If we miss the agreed delivery deadline, or the final delivery is materially incomplete versus the agreed scope, you get a full refund. No negotiation, no credit note. The only exceptions are delays caused by the client: late questionnaire submission or scope changes after commencement.</p></div></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Why is there a RM290 entry offer? Is the quality lower?<span class="faq-ico"></span></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. The entry offer exists to remove the risk of the first transaction. The RM290 logo mark uses the same methodology and team as a RM30,000 architecture project. The difference is scope, not quality. Most clients who start at RM290 move to a larger engagement within 60 days.</p></div></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>How long does a typical project take?<span class="faq-ico"></span></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Entry offers deliver in 7 days. Growth tier projects deliver in 2 to 4 weeks. Full brand architecture and app builds have defined timelines agreed at kickoff, typically 6 to 16 weeks. The clock starts from questionnaire submission, not from payment.</p></div></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Do you work with clients outside Kuala Lumpur?<span class="faq-ico"></span></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. The majority of our process is fully remote by design. Kickoff, reviews, and delivery happen via WhatsApp, email, and video call. We have active clients across Peninsular Malaysia, East Malaysia, and Singapore. In-person sessions are available for Klang Valley clients on request.</p></div></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>What payment methods do you accept?<span class="faq-ico"></span></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>We accept bank transfer, ToyyibPay, and DuitNow QR. For projects above RM5,000 we offer a 50/30/20 split: 50% to start, 30% at the halfway milestone, 20% on final delivery. Full upfront is not required for larger projects.</p></div></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>What is Methodas and do I need it?<span class="faq-ico"></span></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Methodas is our systems and education platform for founders who want to build without hiring an agency full-time. It gives you access to the same frameworks we use for clients. If you want it done for you, Brand Method is for you. If you want to learn and build yourself, Methodas is for you. Many clients use both.</p></div></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>How many revisions do I get?<span class="faq-ico"></span></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Every project includes a defined number of revision rounds in the scope. Entry offers include one round. Growth and premium tiers include two to three. Revisions are based on the original brief. Direction changes after commencement are treated as scope changes and priced separately.</p></div></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>How is Brand Method different from Fiverr?<span class="faq-ico"></span></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Fiverr delivers an asset. Brand Method delivers a system. You get a dedicated PM, a written guarantee, a defined timeline, a growth pathway, and a Malaysian team that understands the local market and SME landscape specifically. The strategy behind the asset is what separates them.</p></div></details></div></div></div></section>
<section class="pr-sec prm-sec"><div class="section-inner">
